  "lessons": [
    {
      "title": "Get knitting!",
      "slug": "get-knitting",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 801,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "920197540",
              "title": null,
              "legacyComponentId": 9662,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "The first time every machine knitter attempts stranded knitting they are amazed. No matter if you are using a manual or automatic patterning machine, knitting 2 colors to create a decorative stitch pattern seems magical.<br>Let's review some of the pitfalls and considerations when knitting fairisle your machine.<br>From tension to floats to stitch pattern design, there are a lot of thing to consider for success with this technique.<br><b><h3>The Goal of this Workshop</h3></b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Encourage you to try the different techniques </li>\r\n<li>Learn and master the settings for YOUR machine</li>\r\n<li>Build your confidence in using Fairisle stitch patterns</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9663,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "LIVE Replay",
          "slug": "live-replay",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6305,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Basics",
      "slug": "the-basics",
      "displayOrder": 2,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 796,
        "lessonOrder": 2
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "exerciseAccordion",
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Knit a sample in fairisle",
                  "bodyHtml": "<style>\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px 50px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n\r\n        max-width: 500px;\r\n        margin: auto;\r\n        background-color: #DCDCDC;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Choose a simple fairisle pattern and 2 contrasting colors.</li>\r\n<li>Cast on and set your machine for fairisle</li>\r\n<li>Knit 4-6\"</li><li>\r\nManual machines use 1x1 needle pusher</li>\r\n<li>Bind off or continue knitting</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div><h3>\r\n<span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"1x1 fairisle\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/1x1_1.jpg\"><i class=\"fa fa-picture-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Sample</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/1x1_2.jpg\" width=\"200\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/119/arrow1.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Experiment with Variations  (Double High)",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\n    \r\n\r\n        Depending on your machine, set machine to knit double high.<ul>\r\n            <li> Punchcard machines will have a lever.</li>\r\n            <li> Electronic machines can be programmed.</li>\r\n            <li> Manual machines, repeat needle selection for 2 rows</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li>Cast on (or continue knitting) and set your machine to \"Double High\"</li>\r\n                <li>Knit for 3-4\"</li>\r\n                <li>Bind off or continue knitting</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n       <h3> <span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"double-high variation\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/double_high1.jpg\"><i class=\"fa fa-picture-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Sample</span></h3>\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/double_high.jpg\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/119/arrow2.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Experiment with Variations  (Double Wide)",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\n    \r\n\r\n        Depending on your machine, set machine to knit double wide.<ul>\r\n            <li> Punchcard machines may not have this feature.</li>\r\n            <li> Electronic machines can be programmed.</li>\r\n            <li> Manual machines, select with 2x2 needle pusher</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li>Cast on (or continue knitting) and set your machine to \"Double Wide\" (if available)</li>\r\n                <li>Knit for 3-4\"</li>\r\n                <li>Bind off or continue knittting</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n      <h3>      <span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"double wide variation\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/double_wide_1.jpg\"><i class=\"fa fa-picture-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\r\n        </div>\r\n</i> Sample</span></h3>\r\n    \r\n    <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/double_wide.jpg\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/119/arrow3.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Vertical Stripes",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\n    \r\n\r\n        Depending on your machine, lock the pattern on a single row so it will repeat and not advance <ul>\r\n            <li> Not all machines have this functionality</li>\r\n\r\n            <li> Manual machines, select the same needles for every row </li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        <div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li>Cast on (or continue knitting) and lock the pattern on a single row so it will repeat and not advance (if available)</li>\r\n                <li>Knit for 3-4\"</li>\r\n                <li> Set the machine for double wide (if available) and repeat the stripes for 3-4\" </li>\r\n                <li>Bind off or continue knitting</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <br>This \"lock\" technique can be used with any stitch pattern, creating stripes of varying widths<br>\r\n    \r\n    \r\n        <img class=\"img-thumbnail zoom\" width=\"200\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/vertical_1x1_stripea.jpg\"><br>\r\n        <img class=\"img-thumbnail zoom\" width=\"200\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/vertical_2x2_stripea.jpg\">\r\n    \r\n\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/119/arrow4.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Swatching is NOT Optional!",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\n        \r\n\r\n           <i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>  From our blog: <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/blog/1145/swatching-with-stitch-patterns\"><b> Swatching in pattern</b></a>\r\n            <div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n                <ol>\r\n                    <li>Cast on for a swatch and knit a few rows in pattern</li>\r\n                    <li>Knit a marker row (change colors or weave a strand of contrasting yarn)</li>\r\n                    <li>Knit Rows for your machine, marking stitch count section <em><small>(see below)</small></em></li>\r\n                    <li>Knit a marker row as before</li>\r\n                    <li>Knit a few rows in pattern</li>\r\n                    <li>bind off or continue knitting</li>\r\n                </ol>\r\n            </div><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n            <table class=\"table table-bordered\">\r\n                <tr>\r\n                    <td>\r\n                        For 4.5 Standard Gauge Machines</td>\r\n                    <td>Isolate 40 stitches and 60 rows</td>\r\n                </tr>\r\n                <tr>\r\n                    <td>For Mid-gauge Machines</td>\r\n                    <td>Isolate 30 stitches and 40 rows</td>\r\n                </tr>\r\n                <tr>\r\n                    <td>\r\n                        For 9.0 Bulky Gauge Machines</td>\r\n                    <td>Isolate 20 stitches and 30 rows</td>\r\n                </tr>\r\n            </table>\r\n        \r\n\r\n\r\n        <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/swatch.jpg\">\r\n        \r\n\r\n    ",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/119/arrow5.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Gauge and Texture",
                  "bodyHtml": "<style>\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px 50px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n\r\n        max-width: 500px;\r\n        margin: auto;\r\n        background-color: #DCDCDC;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n        Fairisle knitting not only has a different gauge than stockinette, but the weight, \"feel\" and texture are very different.<br><div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li>Cast on and knit with a single strand for 4-5\" in stockinette</li>\r\n                <li>Add a 2nd color and knit 2-3\" in fairisle</li>\r\n                <li>Finish the sample with 4-5\" of stockinette</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div><br>\r\n        <span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Notice the difference in gauge and the difference in texture</span><br>If mixing plain knitting (stockinette) with fairisle (or other multi-color stitch patterns) plan to even out the texture. For example, fairisle front and back and solid main color sleeves.<br><b>Suggestions:</b><br>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>Knit the sleeves in the fairisle pattern with 2 strands of the main color</li>\r\n            <li> Knit the sleeves in slip stitch to add bulk and texture similar to the fairisle section</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        \r\n        <h3>      \r\n<span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"Lady Leopard Cardigan\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/lady_leopard_plus1.jpg\"><i class=\"fa fa-picture-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Sample</span></h3>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n      <img class=\"img-thumbnail ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/119/gauge_difference.jpg\">\r\n\r\n    \r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/119/arrow6.png"
                }
              ],
              "legacy": {
                "showText": "below",
                "size": null
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 9652,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
