              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .x3box {\r\n        border: 1px solid #ccc;\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n        margin: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\nHand knitters would be jealous if they knew how easy and fast it is for us to add texture and color to our knitting.<i class=\"fa fa-smile-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><br>Below are some Machine Knit-ables, inspiration from the hand knitting world.<br><span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size: 1.5em;\">Use Fairisle for pillows and folded scarves. The floats are hidden inside </span><br>\r\n\r\nWhatever machine you are using, discovering your favorite stitch patterns and techniques and learning the possibilities—as well as the buttons and levers you need to use to make them happen—are all important parts of the learning curve.\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n        <div class=\"x3box text-center\">\r\n            <h4><b>Diamond Back Pillow</b></h4> <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/path/images/4098/diamond_back_thumb.jpg\">\r\n            <div class=\"text-center\"></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    \r\n    \r\n        <div class=\"x3box text-center\">\r\n            <h4><b>Clacton Scarf</b></h4> <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/path/images/247/clacton_thumb.jpg\">\r\n            <div class=\"text-center\"></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    \r\n    \r\n        <div class=\"x3box text-center\">\r\n            <h4><b>Tomte Pillow</b></h4> <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/path/images/150/santapillowpatternki.jpg\">\r\n            <div class=\"text-center\"></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    \r\n\r\n",
